{"name":"Royal Blue","hex":"#4169e1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"royal blue","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep, bright blue colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep, bright blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/royal_blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Royal blue","blocks":[{"text":"Royal blue is a deep and vivid shade of blue. Traditionally, royal blue is a deep shade of blue and is used in several national flags. However, the web color named royal blue is a much brighter shade."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_blue"},{"title":"Royal Blue (train)","blocks":[{"text":"The Royal Blue was the Baltimore and Ohio Railroad (B&O)'s flagship passenger train between New York City and Washington, D.C., in the United States, beginning in 1890. The Baltimore-based B&O also used the name between 1890 and 1917 for its improved passenger service between New York and Washington, collectively dubbed the Royal Blue Line. Using variants such as the Royal Limited and Royal Special for individual Royal Blue trains, the B&O operated the service in partnership with the Reading Railroad and the Central Railroad of New Jersey. Principal intermediate cities served were Philadelphia, Wilmington, and Baltimore. Later, as Europe reeled from the carnage of World War I and connotations of European royalty fell into disfavor, the B&O discreetly omitted the sobriquet Royal Blue Line from its New York passenger service and the Royal Blue disappeared from B&O timetables. Beginning in 1917, former Royal Blue Line trains were renamed: the Royal Limited, for example, became the National Limited, continuing west from Washington to St. Louis via Cincinnati. During the Depression, the B&O hearkened back to the halcyon pre-World War I era when it launched a re-christened Royal Blue train between New York and Washington in 1935. The B&O finally discontinued all passenger service north of Baltimore on April 26, 1958, including the Royal Blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/B%26O_Royal_Blue_in_1937.jpg/330px-B%26O_Royal_Blue_in_1937.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Blue_(train)"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/B%26O_Royal_Blue_in_1898.jpg/500px-B%26O_Royal_Blue_in_1898.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/B%26O_Royal_Blue_in_1898.jpg/500px-B%26O_Royal_Blue_in_1898.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Royal Limited in 1898, one of the B&O's famed Royal Blue trains","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AB%26O_Royal_Blue_in_1898.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Royal_Blue_Line_ad.jpg/500px-Royal_Blue_Line_ad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Royal_Blue_Line_ad.jpg/1280px-Royal_Blue_Line_ad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Royal_Blue_Line_ad.jpg/500px-Royal_Blue_Line_ad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Royal Blue advertisement, c. 1898","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoyal_Blue_Line_ad.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Royal_Blue_Line_%28advertisement%2C_McClure%27s_Jan_1896%29.jpg/500px-Royal_Blue_Line_%28advertisement%2C_McClure%27s_Jan_1896%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Royal_Blue_Line_%28advertisement%2C_McClure%27s_Jan_1896%29.jpg/1280px-Royal_Blue_Line_%28advertisement%2C_McClure%27s_Jan_1896%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Royal_Blue_Line_%28advertisement%2C_McClure%27s_Jan_1896%29.jpg/500px-Royal_Blue_Line_%28advertisement%2C_McClure%27s_Jan_1896%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoyal_Blue_Line_(advertisement%2C_McClure's_Jan_1896).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Mt_Royal_Station_in_1896_%28Baltimore%29.jpg/500px-Mt_Royal_Station_in_1896_%28Baltimore%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Mt_Royal_Station_in_1896_%28Baltimore%29.jpg/500px-Mt_Royal_Station_in_1896_%28Baltimore%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMt_Royal_Station_in_1896_(Baltimore).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Mount_Royal_St